{
  "title": "Albumin\u2013globulin interaction does not improve cross-sample DSST prediction beyond separate proteins and their ratio",
  "abstract": "In 1,288 NHANES 2011\u20132012 adults aged 60+ and 1,502 separately sampled 2013\u20132014 adults, adding a centered albumin\u2013globulin interaction beyond flexible separate proteins, their ratio and covariates increased validation weighted MSE by 0.782403 score\u00b2 (0.482%). The source-refit/target PSU-bootstrap 95% interval was [-0.718127, 2.559372]. This specific feature did not demonstrate incremental predictive benefit; equivalence and general absence of joint protein information are not established.",
  "keywords": [
    "albumin",
    "globulin",
    "DSST",
    "NHANES",
    "incremental prediction",
    "negative result"
  ],
